  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix \n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's start by writing the matrix $Q-\\lambda I:$\n\ufeff\ufeff\ufeff\n\n$$\nQ-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 7 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-7\\cdot 7 & =0 \\\\ 4-2\\lambda -2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-49 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -45 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+4\\cdot 1\\cdot 45}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{196}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 14}{2} \\\\  & =-5,9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =9.$",
